  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Four empires fell at once and nobody knows who won. The Hittites, Ugarit, Mycenaean Greece, gone inside about one generation.",
        "visual_query": "bronze age ruins eastern mediterranean",
        "visual_fallback": "ancient ruins"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Egypt survived and carved the story. Nine groups are named: Peleset, Sherden, Shekelesh, Denyen. Sea Peoples is a modern label.",
        "visual_query": "egyptian temple relief carved warriors",
        "visual_fallback": "temple relief"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Merneptah claimed six thousand killed and nine thousand taken in his fifth year. Pharaohs exaggerate, but they do not invent whole enemies.",
        "visual_query": "medinet habu hieroglyph wall egypt",
        "visual_fallback": "hieroglyph wall"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Ramesses III fought them in years five, eight and twelve. His inscription lists lands already cut off: Hatti, Carchemish, Alashiya.",
        "visual_query": "nile delta reeds ancient egypt",
        "visual_fallback": "nile reeds"
      },
      {
        "narration": "So here is the turn. Recent work reads them as refugees running from a collapse already happening, not the thing that caused it.",
        "visual_query": "wooden boats mediterranean coast dusk",
        "visual_fallback": "wooden boats"
      }
    ],
